WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.038
Sixty-six thousand dead in World War I. Forty-five thousand four hundred in World War II.

00:00:05.988 --> 00:00:08.829
Five hundred and sixteen in Korea.

00:00:08.829 --> 00:00:12.011
One hundred and sixty-five in Afghanistan.

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:18.102
Seventy-seven thousand and counting from MAID — medical assistance in dying — since 2016.

00:00:18.102 --> 00:00:24.772
Canada's state-administered death program has now killed more Canadians than the Kaiser, Hitler, and the Taliban combined.

00:00:24.772 --> 00:00:27.477
This is fifth-generation warfare.

00:00:27.477 --> 00:00:29.056
No tanks.

00:00:29.056 --> 00:00:30.670
No bombs.

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:32.659
No declarations.

00:00:32.659 --> 00:00:39.034
The weapons are institutional capture, identity erosion, and the normalization of state violence through policy.

00:00:39.034 --> 00:00:45.511
The Truth and Reconciliation Commission collected seven thousand testimonies and issued ninety-four Calls to Action.

00:00:45.511 --> 00:00:49.556
Two hundred and fifteen unmarked graves were announced at Kamloops.

00:00:49.556 --> 00:00:56.965
The pattern is consistent — the state inflicts harm, acknowledges it decades later, and then builds new systems to inflict new harm.

00:00:56.965 --> 00:00:59.227
This is not incompetence.

00:00:59.227 --> 00:01:02.738
This is a war on the population — waged from within.
